# Clean product URLs: /memorials/<slug> serves memorial.html.
#
# The destination MUST be the clean form `/memorial` (not `/memorial.html`).
# Cloudflare Pages applies `.html` canonicalisation to rewrite targets — if
# we point at `/memorial.html` the edge 308-redirects the browser to
# `/memorial`, which strips the `:slug` and breaks the page. Using the
# clean URL keeps the response a true rewrite (status 200, address bar
# unchanged) so memorial.html can read the slug from the path.
#
# Do NOT add a `/memorial -> /memorials` redirect: memorial.html already
# handles the "no slug" case gracefully by showing "Product not found".
/memorials/:slug   /memorial   200

# Partner desk lives on the dedicated Worker (partner.searsmelvin.co.uk).
# Static assets win over these rules if a matching file exists — partner.html
# must stay deleted. Pages Functions for /partner* also 301 ( _redirects is
# not applied to Function-served responses).
/partner.html      https://partner.searsmelvin.co.uk/  301
/partner           https://partner.searsmelvin.co.uk/  301
/partner/          https://partner.searsmelvin.co.uk/  301
/partner/*         https://partner.searsmelvin.co.uk/  301

# Permit checker retired (Oct 2026). Static file removed so these rules apply.
/permit-checker        /memorials  301
/permit-checker.html   /memorials  301
/permit-checker/       /memorials  301

# Typed quote links. The form lives on /contact. Each path is its own 301
# so a trailing slash is not a second hop. The target has no query string,
# so Pages appends the incoming one (same as /index.html and /permit-checker).
# /contact/ is a separate 308 to /contact, so the target stays slash-free.
/request-a-quote       /contact  301
/request-a-quote/      /contact  301
/request-quote         /contact  301
/request-quote/        /contact  301

# /index.html is the same document as /. Keep the query string (Pages
# appends it when the target has none) so a tagged brochure landing
# does not lose its UTMs. Brochure URLs themselves are not redirected.
/index.html    /  301

# Borough cemetery pages are served by functions/areas/[[path]].js.
# _redirects does not apply to a Pages Function, so /areas and
# /areas/<borough> are not listed here. Any other /areas/* path is
# answered by that Function with a 301 to /memorials.
# /areas.html is not a Function route, so it still redirects to the hub.
/areas.html   /areas  301
